WEBVTT

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:01.800
How long do you have? Ten

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:03.100
seconds, a minute, five

00:00:02.967 --> 00:00:04.000
minutes, or ten.

00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:05.100
Software engineer in Pune. I

00:00:04.967 --> 00:00:05.933
build data pipelines by day,

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:06.700
run ultras at dawn, climb

00:00:06.567 --> 00:00:07.500
Sahyadri forts on weekends,

00:00:07.367 --> 00:00:08.267
and write in English and

00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:08.500
Marathi.

00:00:08.633 --> 00:00:09.633
The engineer: 25 projects

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:10.567
shipped, Data pipelines by

00:00:10.433 --> 00:00:11.433
day. The runner: 26 races,

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:12.333
598 km on race day. The

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:13.233
trekker: 20 Sahyadri forts,

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:14.300
Some take two hours. One took

00:00:14.167 --> 00:00:15.200
twenty-two.. The reader and

00:00:15.067 --> 00:00:16.000
writer: 52 books, 22 in

00:00:15.867 --> 00:00:16.933
Marathi, 112 essays · 1,677

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:17.767
short posts. The citizen:

00:00:17.633 --> 00:00:18.767
Technology policy, studied in

00:00:18.633 --> 00:00:19.733
public, Tools that work in

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:20.000
Marathi.

00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:21.133
How I work: Every number has

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:21.900
a source. Accessibility is

00:00:21.767 --> 00:00:22.633
the floor, not a feature.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:23.533
Built for the people who use

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:24.367
it. Phones on slow networks

00:00:24.233 --> 00:00:25.100
first. Ship in days, then

00:00:24.967 --> 00:00:25.767
keep going. Privacy by

00:00:25.633 --> 00:00:26.000
default.

00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:28.867
Read me in ten seconds, or

00:00:28.733 --> 00:00:30.000
ten minutes.
